Build a canonical-directory-to-owner index once during graph construction, preserving current containment and symlink semantics. Each edge then needs a target canonicalization and indexed lookup. Threads or async would only distribute repeated work. Extend the benchmark shapes to include this supported protocol; the existing Cargo fixture cannot expose it. Raw samples: [isolated pnpm performance](appendices/pnpm-performance-isolated.json). Absolute timings are specific to this machine; the source trace establishes the repeated scan.

**F08 — Policy checks invert an upstream error into success. CONFIRMED.**

`license-boundary` and `features-boundary` both run `! cargo tree ... | grep ...`. A fake Cargo executable printing an error and exiting 42 causes both real Just recipes to exit 0. The license tree or production feature set was never obtained, yet the policy reports success.

Run `cargo tree` as a separately checked operation, then inspect its successful output for prohibited dependencies/features. Adding `pipefail` under the same whole-pipeline negation is insufficient: a failed pipeline would still be inverted. Keep this one shared failure-handling correction across both recipes. Sibling checks `lint-affected` and coverage collection have checked pipelines and were not promoted to findings. Exact captured exits: [policy gate reproduction](appendices/policy-gate-repro.json).

**F09 — Init's recovery advice is unreachable. CONFIRMED.**

When automatic workflow pin resolution fails, init can succeed after writing `callisto.toml`, with “Run `callisto init --workflow` to retry.” Following that command immediately fails E190 because init refuses any existing config. Restoring network availability cannot help: the guard runs before workflow generation. Upgrade regeneration guidance repeats the same impossible route.

Refusing to overwrite config is an explicit policy. Preserve it and provide a usable workflow-only recovery path or accurate concrete instructions. Test first-attempt failure followed by the advertised retry. The finding is contradictory guidance, not a demand for automatic overwrites. Evidence: [DX appendix](appendices/dx.md).

**F10 — JSON decoding loses file provenance. CONFIRMED.**

`read_json_input` merges inline input, stdin and files into a bare string. All JSON parse failures become E281, classified as Usage. A malformed snapshot/decision file therefore returns exit 2 without its filename, although the stability contract classifies invalid file content as runtime failure. `compose-pr-body --preview` independently maps its file parse into the same usage variant. The control `release inspect --input` returns exit 1 with E238 for the same malformed file.

Carry input origin/path through decoding and error classification. Reuse broad diagnostics where possible; permanent new flags/error codes are unnecessary for this correction. Exercise the same malformed bytes via inline/file/stdin and assert the intended classification. Relative `--snapshot`/`--decision` behavior is also inconsistent with most file flags, but its exact published contract is nuanced and it was not counted as a confirmed defect. Evidence: [DX appendix](appendices/dx.md).

