**F08 — Policy checks invert an upstream error into success. CONFIRMED.**

`license-boundary` and `features-boundary` both run `! cargo tree ... | grep ...`. A fake Cargo executable printing an error and exiting 42 causes both real Just recipes to exit 0. The license tree or production feature set was never obtained, yet the policy reports success.

Run `cargo tree` as a separately checked operation, then inspect its successful output for prohibited dependencies/features. Adding `pipefail` under the same whole-pipeline negation is insufficient: a failed pipeline would still be inverted. Keep this one shared failure-handling correction across both recipes. Sibling checks `lint-affected` and coverage collection have checked pipelines and were not promoted to findings. Exact captured exits: [policy gate reproduction](appendices/policy-gate-repro.json).

